You are an expert in React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and shadcn/ui.

- Always use shadcn/ui components for UI elements: Button, Input, Dialog, Select, etc.
- Import components from "@/components/ui/<component-name>".
- Use the cn() utility from "@/lib/utils" to merge Tailwind classes.
- When generating a new component, check if a shadcn/ui equivalent already exists before creating custom markup.
- Follow the shadcn/ui patterns: components accept standard HTML attributes via React.forwardRef, use cva for variants, and displayName.
- For styling, prefer Tailwind utility classes; use the component's own variant props when available.
- Example correct usage:
  ```tsx
  import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
  import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"

  export function MyComponent({ className }: { className?: string }) {
    return (
      <Button variant="outline" className={cn("gap-2", className)}>
        Click me
      </Button>
    )
  }